---
description: Kotlin rules for the AutofillService, autofill-core and the RN bridge
globs: apps/mobile/android/**/*.kt,apps/mobile/android/**/*.gradle,apps/mobile/android/**/*.xml
alwaysApply: false
---

- Module direction: :app → :autofill → :autofill-core. `:autofill-core` must not import `android.*`.
- `FillmateModule.kt` (bridge) only translates types/threads and calls `FillmateAutofill` (facade). No logic.
- `FillmateAutofillService` stays thin; decisions go in `FillRequestHandler` and its collaborators.
- Never call the LLM or block on network inside `onFillRequest` beyond the single Tier 2 call with timeout.
- Always complete the FillCallback exactly once; on any error return `onSuccess(null)`.
- Matching rules come from `rules.json` on the classpath. Never hardcode stopwords or qualifiers.
- `ClayTokens.kt` is generated; edit `packages/design-tokens/tokens.json` instead.
- Add Gradle dependencies only in the phase that needs them (`.claude/build-plan.md`); ask first.
- Spec: `.claude/autofill-service.md`, `.claude/matching-pipeline.md`.
